### Architecture of the Multi-Channel Notification System

Our **Notification System** architecture cleanly separates shared notification lifecycle from channel-specific delivery protocols:

```text
               +--------------------------------------+
               |    AbstractNotificationChannel       | (Abstract Class)
               +--------------------------------------+
               | - channelName: String                |
               | + send(Notification): void (final)   |
               | # deliver(Notification): void (abs)  |
               +--------------------------------------+
                                  ^
         +------------------------+------------------------+
         |                                                 |
+----------------------+                  +----------------------+
|  EmailChannel        |                  |  SmsChannel          |
+----------------------+                  +----------------------+
| # deliver(): void    |                  | # deliver(): void    |
+----------------------+                  +----------------------+
```

**System Responsibilities:**
1. **`Notification` Model**: Value object containing recipient, subject, and message content.
2. **`AbstractNotificationChannel`**: Abstract class providing standard validation, audit logging, and the template dispatch method.
3. **Concrete Channels**: `EmailChannel`, `SmsChannel`, and `PushChannel` implement specialized network delivery.

---

### Executable Notification Engine Implementation

```java
class Notification {
    private final String recipient;
    private final String message;

    public Notification(String recipient, String message) {
        this.recipient = recipient;
        this.message = message;
    }

    public String getRecipient() { return recipient; }
    public String getMessage() { return message; }
}

abstract class AbstractNotificationChannel {
    private final String channelName;

    public AbstractNotificationChannel(String channelName) {
        this.channelName = channelName;
    }

    // Template method: invariant workflow
    public final void dispatch(Notification notification) {
        if (notification == null || notification.getRecipient().isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid notification recipient");
        }
        System.out.println("[" + channelName + "] Audit: Dispatching alert to " + notification.getRecipient());
        deliver(notification);
    }

    // Abstract hook: implemented by concrete channel
    protected abstract void deliver(Notification notification);
}

class EmailChannel extends AbstractNotificationChannel {
    public EmailChannel() { super("EMAIL"); }

    @Override
    protected void deliver(Notification notification) {
        System.out.println("  -> Transmitting SMTP packet: " + notification.getMessage());
    }
}

class SmsChannel extends AbstractNotificationChannel {
    public SmsChannel() { super("SMS"); }

    @Override
    protected void deliver(Notification notification) {
        System.out.println("  -> Sending SMS via cellular gateway: " + notification.getMessage());
    }
}

public class NotificationApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Notification alert = new Notification("dev-team@enterprise.com", "Cluster health check: 100% OK");

        AbstractNotificationChannel[] channels = { new EmailChannel(), new SmsChannel() };
        for (AbstractNotificationChannel channel : channels) {
            channel.dispatch(alert);
        }
    }
}
```

**Console Output:**
```text
[EMAIL] Audit: Dispatching alert to dev-team@enterprise.com
  -> Transmitting SMTP packet: Cluster health check: 100% OK
[SMS] Audit: Dispatching alert to dev-team@enterprise.com
  -> Sending SMS via cellular gateway: Cluster health check: 100% OK
```

---

### Extensibility Verification

Adding Slack, Microsoft Teams, or Webhook channels requires zero modification to `NotificationApp` or `AbstractNotificationChannel`.

